### Quick3DLineTool.ts
0001: /**
0002:  * Quick3DLineTool - Automatic 3D line creation from predefined projections
0003:  * 
0004:  * Creates a complete 3D line immediately using fixed coordinates:
0005:  * - P_H projection: L_H from (0, 0) to (50, 50) - diagonal line
0006:  * - P_V projection: L_V from (0, 0) to (50, 50) - diagonal line
0007:  * - 3D line: Line3DFromProjections through origin with direction (1, 1, 1)
0008:  * 
0009:  * Geometric relationship:
0010:  * - P_H maps (u,v) → (x=u, y=v, z=0)
0011:  * - L_H has direction (1,1) in P_H → direction (1,1,0) in 3D
0012:  * - P_V maps (u,v) → (x=u, y=0, z=v)
0013:  * - L_V has direction (1,1) in P_V → direction (1,0,1) in 3D
0014:  * - Reconstructed 3D line: direction (1,1,1), through origin
0015:  * 
0016:  * Useful for:
0017:  * - Quick testing without manual projection creation (~100x faster than manual)
0018:  * - Creating consistent example 3D lines for demo/screenshots
0019:  * - Demonstrating 3D line from projections concept
0020:  * 
0021:  * Pattern: Similar to QuickProjectionSetupTool (immediate execution)
0022:  * Related: Create3DLineTool (interactive, user selects existing lines)
0023:  * 
0024:  * Phase 105
0025:  */
0026: 
